  "question": {
    "text": "Let the parabola $y=x^2+\\mathrm{p} x-3$, meet the coordinate axes at the points $\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{Q}$ and R . If the circle C with centre at $(-1,-1)$ passes through the points $P, Q$ and $R$, then the area of $\\triangle P Q R$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CnZ5W",
      "text": "$7$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "G97Gp",
      "text": "$4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "swXzK",
      "text": "$6$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "8TW9q",
      "text": "$5$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{y}=\\mathrm{x}^2+\\mathrm{px}-3$\n\nLet $\\mathrm{P}(\\alpha, 0), \\mathrm{Q}(\\beta, 0), \\mathrm{R}(0,-3)$\nCircle with centre $(-1,-1)$ is $(x+1)^2+(y+1)^2=r^2$\nPasses through $(0,-3)$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\left.1^2+(-2)^2=r^2\\right] \\\\\n& \\mathrm{r}^2=5\n\\end{aligned}$\n$(x+1)^2+(y+1)^2=5$\n\nPut $\\mathrm{y}=0$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& (x+1)^2=5-1 \\\\\n& (x+1)^2=4 \\\\\n& x+1= \\pm 2 \\\\\n& x=1 \\text { or } x=-3 \\\\\n& \\therefore P(1,0) \\text { and } Q(-3,0)\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nArea of $\\triangle \\mathrm{PQR}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{array}\\right|=6$",
    "image": null
  },
